    {
      "text": "even the very God of Israel do men trample, 1 Ne. 19:7. arise from the dust, my sons, and be men, 2 Ne. 1:21. men are instructed sufficiently that they know good from evil, 2 Ne. 2:5. days of the children of men were prolonged, 2 Ne. 2:21. Adam fell that men might be, 2 Ne. 2:25. men are free according to the flesh, 2 Ne. 2:27. that he may draw all men unto him, 2 Ne. 26:24 (3 Ne. 27:14). gone astray … by the precepts of men, 2 Ne. 28:14. persuade all men not to rebel against God, Jacob 1:8. have just men to be your kings, Mosiah 23:8. it shall be made known unto just and holy men, Alma 13:26. he granteth unto men according to their desire, Alma 29:4. he imparteth his word … not only men but women also, Alma 32:23. this life is the time for men to prepare to meet God, Alma 34:32. whether there is more than one time appointed for men to rise, Alma 40:8. if all men had been … like unto Moroni, Alma 48:17. what manner of men ought ye to be, 3 Ne. 27:27. I give unto men weakness that they may be humble, Ether 12:27. my grace is sufficient for all men, Ether 12:27.",
